From b0023fcdc52a826cade8fb225255d77c0640ee4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:57:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: avoid the AR50 AXI halt sequence on IRIS1

IRIS1 uses HFI4 packets but not the AR50 wrapper AXI halt sequence.
The VPU5 downstream suspend path waits for firmware power-collapse
readiness, sends the secure suspend request, then disables resources.
It does not access WRAPPER_CPU_AXI_HALT or poll its AR50 status bit.

Skip only that legacy MMIO sequence for IRIS1 after the existing secure
suspend call succeeds. Keep the HFI idle/PC_READY checks and SCM error
handling, as well as all other VPU paths.

Reference: Android Q venus_hfi.c __suspend(), __venus_power_off() and
__power_collapse(), downstream 192eca8550f95c.

This changes power-down behavior and requires idle/resume and repeated
session testing on hardware before any stability claim. It does not
replace a proper SM8150 clock/reset/power-domain resource description.

Signed-off-by: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
index e59e11c65..f3060e1eb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
@@ -581,7 +581,8 @@ static int venus_halt_axi(struct venus_hfi_device *hdev)
 	u32 mask_val;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (IS_AR50_LITE(hdev->core))
+	/* VPU5 powers down after the firmware/SCM suspend handshake. */
+	if (IS_IRIS1(hdev->core) || IS_AR50_LITE(hdev->core))
 		return 0;
 
 	if (IS_IRIS2(hdev->core) || IS_IRIS2_1(hdev->core)) {
